# oracle: native binary restart of dihedral charmm with improper cvff, and lj/charmm/coul/charmm (dihedral_charmm.cpp k, multiplicity, shift, weight, weightflag; improper_cvff.cpp k, sign, multiplicity); 16 chains of 6 atoms (atom_style full, dihedral.data with bonds, angles, dihedrals and impropers), 50 steps written natively, then read and continued for 100 steps
# oracle-inputs: w185nr_dihedral_charmm.restart
# native: b332f28 built as the parity binary wrote w185nr_dihedral_charmm.restart (lj/cut or lj/charmm/coul/charmm pair with zero epsilon)
read_restart    w185nr_dihedral_charmm.restart
neighbor        0.3 bin
thermo_style    custom step temp epair ebond eangle edihed eimp etotal press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          50
fix             1 all nve
run             100
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-9 abs=1e-12
# measured: max relative error 2.8e-14 (native restart continuation, engine vs native thermo and per-atom), so the tolerance is 1e-9
